.policy "ruff-int001-f-string-in-get-text-func-call" revision 2
.description "Pass a constant template to a gettext call and format the translated result; an f-string is evaluated before the catalog lookup."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff INT001 (flake8-gettext): a translation call whose first positional argument is an f-string (or adjacent literals one of which is). The text is
// formatted before the catalog lookup, so the lookup is for the formatted string, which no catalog has.
// Translation calls: a plain name in option `flake8-gettext.function-names` (default `_`, `gettext`, `ngettext`; plus
// `extend-function-names`), `builtins.<one of them>`, and gettext.gettext / gettext.ngettext through imports.
// Ruff checks ngettext's second argument only in preview.
//   _(f"Hello, {name}!")                  ← INT001
//   gettext_mod.gettext(f"{x}")            ← INT001, after `import gettext as gettext_mod`
//   _(t"{x}")                              not reported: a t-string
//   _gettext(f"{x}")                       not reported: not a translation name
#include "python/misc2-messages.rr"

.violation INT001(at: node) code "INT001"
    "Translate a constant template, then format the result: `_(\"Hello, %s!\") % name`, not `_(f\"Hello, {{name}}!\")`. Leave it if the callee is not a translation function or the text is a computed catalog key."
    suppress ruff "INT001"
INT001(a) :- msg_gettext(c), msg_arg(c, 0, a), msg_form(a, "fstr").
